               15:30  TOTAL time spent

Once I understood the various components of the starter code, the implementation
was quite straightforward and the only thing I considered tricky was designing
the functions around suitable abstractions for future work (e.g., retries).
Instead, I spent a great deal of time thinking about how I would test my service.
I tried to cover many cases I could think of in terms of unit testing and
end-to-end functionality, but there were some things I chose not to test because 
they seemed implementation-specific rather than part of the specification. 
Moreover, I struggled testing some non-deterministic aspects of the code such
as ensuring the average latency fluctuates properly, since it is quite difficult
to prove an upper bound on latencies (CPUs can throttle, the scheduler can
interfere, etc).
